# Terraform standards

Canonical detail: `AGENTS.md`.

- All AWS infrastructure is code under `terraform/bootstrap/` (one-time) and `terraform/envs/prod/` (ongoing). Modules live in `terraform/modules/`.
- **No console-driven resource changes.** Wire secrets through Secrets Manager resources and ECS task definitions — never commit secret values or AWS account IDs.
- Prefer `data.aws_caller_identity` over hardcoded account IDs. GitHub OIDC trust pins immutable owner/repo numeric IDs (not secrets, but do not invent new ones casually).
- CI already runs via `.github/workflows/terraform.yml` (fmt, validate, tflint, plan on PR; apply on `main` with `environment: production`). Do not add another Terraform workflow.
- Edits under `terraform/**` fire Terraform CI; successful apply on `main` can chain to **Deploy Web**. Keep infra PRs intentional and small.
- Before finishing: `terraform fmt -check -recursive terraform/`, `make validate` / local `terraform validate`, and tflint when available.
